20. DATABASE SECURITY AND ROW LEVEL SECURITY
==================================================

Implement proper Supabase RLS.

Rules:

CITIZENS:
- Can insert their own complaints.
- Can read their own complaints.
- Can update only permitted non-administrative fields of their own reports.
- Cannot change complaint status or priority.
- Cannot assign workers.
- Cannot access other citizens' private information.

ADMINISTRATORS:
- Can review complaints.
- Can manage categories.
- Can assign workers.
- Can approve resolutions.
- Can view operational analytics.
- Can manage authorized user roles through controlled database operations.

FIELD WORKERS:
- Can view their own assigned tasks.
- Can submit work progress.
- Can upload evidence for assigned tasks.
- Cannot approve their own resolutions.
- Cannot access unrelated citizen information.

IMPORTANT:
- Enable RLS on every relevant table.
- Never trust role values received from the frontend.
- Prevent users from editing their own role.
- Use secure PostgreSQL functions for privileged state transitions.
- Validate worker assignments inside database functions.
- Avoid unrestricted anonymous write access.
- Never expose the Supabase service_role key.

